<title>USA: Lilly, Inhale to develop new product.</title>
<headline>Lilly, Inhale to develop new product.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eli LIlly and Co and Inhale Therapeutic Systems said Tuesday they will collaborate to develop a product that will help deliver an osteoporosis drug into the lungs.</p>
<p>Lilly will pay up to $20 million in return for global commercialization rights for the product, which will be based on Inhale's deep-lung delivery system for macromolecules. Inhale, headquartered in Palo Alto,  will manufacture packaged powders for and supply inhalation devices to Lilly, and will receive royalties.</p>
<p>Lilly will lead the clinical trial effort and hopes to begin further human trials in 1997.</p>
</text>
